        "document": {
          "url": "https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/852/21210852/att_857898/v1/et200pro_operating_instructions_en-US_en-US.pdf",
          "title": "ET 200pro distributed I/O system operating instructions",
          "revision": "09/2015, A5E00335544-AJ",
          "pages": "p.94 pin-assignment table; p.258 connection-module identity; p.309 interface-module identity"
        },
        "modelingNotes": [
          "The orderNumber field lists an electronic module plus its required connection module. This is a documented two-part assembly, not a single Siemens order number.",
          "Every exposed field-connector pin is inventoried, including unassigned pins. Terminal keys Xn.p identify connector Xn, physical pin p. Descriptive signal names are not alternative physical terminals.",
          "The internal backplane contacts, module-to-module power distribution, protective behavior and configuration are not modeled. No backplane supply screw terminals are invented.",
          "Connector pin metadata, functions and repeated 1M/2M/FE/Us labels do not join physical nets. Author any verified conductor continuity explicitly. No-connection positions are inventory annotations; a do-not-wire rule is not implemented.",
          "Connector presence is separate from electrical continuity. A cable assembly with an unresolved pin map does not satisfy a required electrical terminal. Unused socket sealing and hardware installation requirements remain project review items.",
          "X03 is the supply feed and X04 is the loop-through. X03 pin 4 (1L+) and pin 2 (1M) are universally required for interface electronics. Load supply 2L+/2M is application-dependent; require it in the project when needed.",
          "Ethernet remains in communication ports only. Verified p.94 physical assignment: X02P1 pins 1/2/3/4 = TD+/RD+/TD-/RD-; X02P2 pins 1/2/3/4 = RD+/TD+/RD-/TD-; connector thread FE. Ethernet signal terminals and thread bonding are documented here but not represented as physical electrical endpoints.",
          "No permanent net tie between X03 and X04 or the internal backplane is asserted by this model. The documented loop-through identity does not yet provide an internal conductive-link primitive."
        ]
      },
      "connectionCoverage": {
        "status": "partial",
        "notes": "All ten X03/X04 power pins and both PROFINET ports are inventoried. Ethernet physical signal/thread endpoints, backplane contacts, internal loop-through continuity and mounting/bonding details are not modeled."
      },
